      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T22:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How should this interact with the existing low power states?  Can/should muxes support both low power and an idle mode? Should we be assuming one is a superset of the other (ex. are all low power modes expected to already cover the requirements for chipset idle)?",
      "revId": "0165f8ab076e36c2fc5bbb7b9707d1d0db7c705c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca405ba2_d6a13963",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T01:59:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the mux chip driver gets to decide. in the case of the\nburnside bridge, the driver can hold the chip in reset and even\npower-gate it on some boards. the BB driver needs to track this\nand ignore system power transitions when that is the case.\nother mux chip drivers could hypothetically not power down\nthe mux for low power mode and only track chipset idle state.",
      "parentUuid": "6a4cb962_1235af13",
      "revId": "0165f8ab076e36c2fc5bbb7b9707d1d0db7c705c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6e21b02_3dd38a3f",
        "filename": "driver/usb_mux/usb_mux.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T14:53:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some of this needs to be decided at the usb_mux.c level though, right? Should a mux in low power mode be woken to put it into idle?  \n\nTo an extent, the driver makes the ultimate decision here, but the usb_mux.c code is already tasked with maintaining the LPM state so it doesn\u0027t make a lot of sense to introduce this API as being disjoint from that",
      "parentUuid": "ca405ba2_d6a13963",
      "revId": "0165f8ab076e36c2fc5bbb7b9707d1d0db7c705c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ead81793_c7befed3",
        "filename": "include/usb_mux.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T22:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Probably specify the expected mux state interactions, similar to how low power mode specifies it happens on disconnect.  \n\nIs this expected to run even when the mux has been in an active mode?  If so, does leaving this mode restore the mux to its previous state or does the common code need to handle that?",
      "revId": "0165f8ab076e36c2fc5bbb7b9707d1d0db7c705c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
